<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.2.2 models alternative process runs as separate flows, again without additional graphical elements. The class is a design decision of this pattern."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#SystemBorder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Grenze, die den Betrachtungshorizont eines Prozesses festlegt. Unter bestimmten Bedingungen kann sie auch als Bilanzgrenze für ein- und ausgehende Produkte und Energien aufgefasst werden."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#TechnicalResource> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
_:Nfdde184482c8461a87302bdb020f82fa <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "An ontology design pattern for the formalised description of technical processes according to VDI/VDE 3682 part 1. A process is described as a network: process operators transform the state of products, energies and information, flows connect the operators, technical resources are assigned to the operators that carry them out, and a system border bounds what is described. Every definition carries the German wording of the standard alongside its English translation. The pattern is one of three subdomain patterns of the AIAS information model and is meant to be imported and aligned rather than used on its own."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> .
_:N7e8b80322981484d96e1daf211b7b152 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Normative basis: VDI/VDE 3682 Part 1 and Part 2, issue May 2015.\r\n\r\nTwelve classes and seven relations. Every definition carries the German wording of the standard alongside its English translation, since the standard is issued bilingually.\r\n\r\nScope: Part 1 in full, and from Part 2 the state as a class of the information model. The attribute structure of Part 2 Section 4.4 is not covered."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Energy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Energie, die von einem Prozessoperator benötigt oder freigesetzt wird, beispielsweise elektrische Energie oder Wärme."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Process> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A network describing a technical process. Its nodes are the states of products, energies and information, its directed edges are the transformation steps carried out by process operators."@en .
_:N69218a96a5ad4eebb21f2f02d8447a8c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:Nb14b9d89f4dd48a09f945e6c520edaaa .
