<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fluss, der Teil eines getrennten Flusses ist und sich gegenseitig ausschließende Prozesswege bezeichnet."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#isInput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "is input of"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A flow that is part of a separate flow denoting mutually exclusive process paths."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 2, Figure 2 carries state as a class of the information model. Part 1 avoids the term in the graphical notation, where the three kinds appear directly."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Flow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Gerichtete Verbindung von Produkten zwischen Prozessoperatoren."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#SystemBorder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Systemgrenze"@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.2. Figure 3 carries this relation as the usage symbol, an edge of the graphical notation. Reifying it as a class is a design decision of this pattern."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Alexander Fay" .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Things of the real world that are transformed within a technical process."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/subject> "Formalised Process Description"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ParallelFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A flow that is part of a partially shared flow denoting process steps running concurrently."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Energy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Energy"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#consistsOf> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Verbindet einen Prozess mit den Elementen, die ihn beschreiben."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Used in two places. A flow carries a state, and a product, an energy or an information has one. The thing is therefore separate from the condition it is in, which is what lets one product appear in a process before and after a transformation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Assignment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Process> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.1, page 8."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Vorgang, durch den der Eingangszustand von Produkten, Energien oder Informationen in einen Ausgangszustand umgewandelt wird."@de .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Flow> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
